derivations.claim:
[(a) representative independence] Let $\varphi=z\psi$ with $z
e0$. By [F3] one has $T_{\varphi,\varphi}=T_{z\psi,z\psi}=|z|^{2}T_{\psi,\psi}$, and by [F5] the squared norms satisfy $\|\varphi\|^{2}=|z|^{2}\|\psi\|^{2}$ with $|z|^{2}
e0$; dividing the first identity by the second gives $T_{\varphi,\varphi}/\|\varphi\|^{2}=T_{\psi,\psi}/\|\psi\|^{2}$, and the second identity of [F3] identifies the common value as $T_{
u(\psi),
u(\psi)}$, which is a pure state by [F2]. Thus the operator depends only on the ray.

